        </div>

        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Zones are a sound framework on a shaky foundation: 220-minus-age misses individuals by
            ten to twelve beats routinely. Treat any calculated zone as a hypothesis, and
            <strong class="text-white">make your easy sessions genuinely easy</strong> — that
            single correction outperforms every other refinement.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Skip the grip sensors; they are least accurate when it matters and require holding the
            rails, which changes the session. The
            <a href="/treadmill-workouts/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">talk test</a>
            is free and self-calibrating. And if you take medication affecting heart rate, get
            your ranges from your doctor rather than a formula.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
